            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for a narrow lane, then the Marathi for a tenement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दूतावास",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दूतावास — dūtāvās — \"an embassy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मीरा व्हिसासाठी दूतावासात गेली. mīrā vhisāsāṭhī dūtāvāsāt gelī. Meera went to the embassy for her visa."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दूत is an envoy and आवास a dwelling: the envoy’s house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दूतावास (dūtāvās) is a modern word built from Sanskrit dūta, \"an envoy\", and āvāsa, \"a dwelling\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
